<p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table B.21</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_79efc528-0696-47aa-ab1f-5c7b0a929e97" id="_79efc528-0696-47aa-ab1f-5c7b0a929e97"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">&#x5433;</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">&#x5973;&#x58EB;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">title</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table B.22</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_89acd974-cfb2-4bb7-9239-c4602fca056f" id="_89acd974-cfb2-4bb7-9239-c4602fca056f"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">&#x912D;</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">&#x91AB;&#x751F;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">title</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table B.23</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_5c7b2284-b830-4315-a3a3-edc1ca7a3570" id="_5c7b2284-b830-4315-a3a3-edc1ca7a3570"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">&#x963F;</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">&#x738B;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;"></td><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_colombian" id="_colombian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.9 Colombian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_czech" id="_czech"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.10 Czech</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_english" id="_english"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.11 English</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3d7364a4-dbe1-438a-8b13-65812da59de3" id="_3d7364a4-dbe1-438a-8b13-65812da59de3"></a>given name(s) (+ optional family name)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_0ab7f810-cc81-47ce-95b4-8d903a09eb87" id="_0ab7f810-cc81-47ce-95b4-8d903a09eb87"></a>English names are names used in, or originating in, England. In England as
elsewhere in the English-speaking world, a complete name usually consists of a
given name, commonly referred to as a first name or Christian name, and a (most
commonly patrilineal) family name or surname, also referred to as a last name.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_90ee3732-f654-4a38-9ed8-383f00de25b6" id="_90ee3732-f654-4a38-9ed8-383f00de25b6"></a>There can be several given names, some of these being often referred to as a
second name, or middle name(s).</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_9edd36c8-951a-4138-821a-e663a15c5f42" id="_9edd36c8-951a-4138-821a-e663a15c5f42"></a>Double-barrelled names, compound surnames in English feature two words,
are often joined by a hyphen or hyphens.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_0ff52799-e06e-4ebc-9992-fac18fee4909" id="_0ff52799-e06e-4ebc-9992-fac18fee4909"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Henry Hepburne-Scott</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8c315dde-dccc-4a0f-a536-681a1e85029d" id="_8c315dde-dccc-4a0f-a536-681a1e85029d"></a>Some families having as many as
three or four words making up their surname.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_14b5caa4-3943-45e5-b196-58555c0fe704" id="_14b5caa4-3943-45e5-b196-58555c0fe704"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Charles Hepburn-Stuart-Forbes-Trefusis, 21st Baron Clinton.</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_6651b5e1-e69b-44db-bcaf-96712bd70621" id="_6651b5e1-e69b-44db-bcaf-96712bd70621"></a>It is not unusual for compound surnames to be composed of separate words
not linked by a hyphen.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_0c12ee0f-8c43-4fd8-a46d-f1e9fcc6484b" id="_0c12ee0f-8c43-4fd8-a46d-f1e9fcc6484b"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Iain Duncan Smith has a surname of &#x201C;Duncan Smith&#x201D;.</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_french" id="_french"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.12 French</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3bd8a921-216b-445c-b359-63045638f90c" id="_3bd8a921-216b-445c-b359-63045638f90c"></a>given name(s) (+ optional family name)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_13794c95-14e3-42c6-be21-f4957a018e56" id="_13794c95-14e3-42c6-be21-f4957a018e56"></a>French people have one, two or more given names (first names). One of them
is used in daily life.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_3df06b54-ec9b-46f3-a0ab-54010216445e" id="_3df06b54-ec9b-46f3-a0ab-54010216445e"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Jacques Chirac&#x201D; instead of officially of Jacques Ren&#xE9; Chirac.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_085ffa4d-bd22-4698-b0a0-5fb2f2266e62" id="_085ffa4d-bd22-4698-b0a0-5fb2f2266e62"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Philippe P&#xE9;tain&#x201D; instead of officially of Henri Philippe P&#xE9;tain,
because Philippe was the given name that he used in daily
life.</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_9d7b9ffe-34e4-4504-b3f7-d573d8a15245" id="_9d7b9ffe-34e4-4504-b3f7-d573d8a15245"></a>Middle names in the English sense do not exist, and middle initials are
never used for second or further given names.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_84ecf07f-d3c9-4f0f-854f-e64f69c2d438" id="_84ecf07f-d3c9-4f0f-854f-e64f69c2d438"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Claude All&#xE8;gre may be cited as &#x201C;Claude J. All&#xE8;gre&#x201D; in English-speaking scientific publications, but not in French ones.</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_german" id="_german"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.13 German</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_48df8373-3463-4b51-9660-c3c5f9376eae" id="_48df8373-3463-4b51-9660-c3c5f9376eae"></a>given name(s) (+ optional family name)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_dfeda377-9ebb-4f84-b234-502180ef0e5a" id="_dfeda377-9ebb-4f84-b234-502180ef0e5a"></a>Personal names in German-speaking Europe consist of one or several given names
(Vorname, plural Vornamen) and a surname (Nachname, Familienname). The Vorname
is usually gender-specific.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3330cdb4-ece2-439a-9306-4c0d9a5a6b91" id="_3330cdb4-ece2-439a-9306-4c0d9a5a6b91"></a>Typical order of &#x201C;given name, surname&#x201D;.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_75c2ffde-4c02-40bb-986e-df8666774c62" id="_75c2ffde-4c02-40bb-986e-df8666774c62"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Otto Eduard Leopold F&#xFC;rst von Bismarck.</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ad1e7837-8886-4036-87ac-80e513d74aeb" id="_ad1e7837-8886-4036-87ac-80e513d74aeb"></a>The Vorname (in English forename) is usually given to a child by the parents
shortly after birth. It is common to give a child several Vornamen (forenames).</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_cbf84182-7642-43a0-8631-7c7348b10e36" id="_cbf84182-7642-43a0-8631-7c7348b10e36"></a>The Rufname (&#x201C;appellation name&#x201D; or &#x201C;call name&#x201D;) is the given name
intended for everyday use, and is often underlined on official documents.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_e7de8a4d-5b5e-4c87-9e99-86ab720fbe77" id="_e7de8a4d-5b5e-4c87-9e99-86ab720fbe77"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>The Rufname of the mathematician Amalie Emmy Noether is &#x201C;Emmy&#x201D;.</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_greek" id="_greek"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.14 Greek</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_hindu" id="_hindu"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.15 Hindu</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_hungarian" id="_hungarian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.16 Hungarian</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_fc5dbf2a-4e49-48dc-9ca9-03aeae6110e8" id="_fc5dbf2a-4e49-48dc-9ca9-03aeae6110e8"></a>family name(s) + given name(s)</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_8735109d-ce78-4089-9733-b6c8759a2809" id="_8735109d-ce78-4089-9733-b6c8759a2809"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>KOVA&#x301;CS Ja&#x301;nos</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b7ced529-4b04-4f45-a0b3-e9d9ad4a6dea" id="_b7ced529-4b04-4f45-a0b3-e9d9ad4a6dea"></a>If there is more than one given name, they come in order of importance
after the family name:</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_df34a807-472c-4b6b-92ee-26c78609f85d" id="_df34a807-472c-4b6b-92ee-26c78609f85d"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>KOVA&#x301;CS Ja&#x301;nos Alada&#x301;r.</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_854775f6-5c3d-4728-aac2-c1bac3923cf2" id="_854775f6-5c3d-4728-aac2-c1bac3923cf2"></a>There can be more than one family name, which can be written fully or abbreviated
into initials:</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_04a03bf7-f9e0-469b-b29d-73318c95c2bc" id="_04a03bf7-f9e0-469b-b29d-73318c95c2bc"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>SEGESDY KOVA&#x301;CS Ja&#x301;nos</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_3c1bf264-9f35-4164-b70e-20897c23e76f" id="_3c1bf264-9f35-4164-b70e-20897c23e76f"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  4</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>SEGESDY-KOVA&#x301;CS Ja&#x301;nos</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_08eccd83-2bad-4335-9b2f-a720ffceb088" id="_08eccd83-2bad-4335-9b2f-a720ffceb088"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  5</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>S.KOVA&#x301;CS Ja&#x301;nos</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_a24e6762-81f1-45e3-9df1-b38a6041713c" id="_a24e6762-81f1-45e3-9df1-b38a6041713c"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  6</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>SEGESDY K. Ja&#x301;nos</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_icelandic" id="_icelandic"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.17 Icelandic</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2150d2ec-1b6f-4c6e-a13a-b1feec051ae0" id="_2150d2ec-1b6f-4c6e-a13a-b1feec051ae0"></a>given name(s) + (patronymic or matronymic) (+ optional genonymic) (+ optional family name)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_09f8357f-68e2-474a-b914-fcc42efc5e62" id="_09f8357f-68e2-474a-b914-fcc42efc5e62"></a>Icelandic names differ from most current Western family name systems by being
patronymic or occasionally matronymic: they indicate the father (or mother) of
the child and not the historic family lineage.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_f03e26f9-673a-49a8-beeb-034993776dae" id="_f03e26f9-673a-49a8-beeb-034993776dae"></a>Iceland&#x2019;s traditional name system was formerly used by all Nordic countries
except partly Finland.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_dc6970bf-f3cb-474a-abe1-d1a01dcfa23f" id="_dc6970bf-f3cb-474a-abe1-d1a01dcfa23f"></a>The Icelandic system is not based on family names
(although some people do have family names and might use both systems).
Generally, a person&#x2019;s second name indicates the first name of their father
(patronymic) or in some cases mother (matronymic). According to Icelandic
naming tradition, second names end in -son or -d&#xF3;ttir with few exceptions.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_db3d260f-0411-404c-84ec-f8406e2df046" id="_db3d260f-0411-404c-84ec-f8406e2df046"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>J&#xF3;hanna Sigur&#xF0;ard&#xF3;ttir. &#x201C;J&#xF3;hanna, daughter of Sigur&#xF0;ur&#x201D;.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_435ba694-f1c1-4196-b101-44fa8599d4a4" id="_435ba694-f1c1-4196-b101-44fa8599d4a4"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Matronymic. Hei&#xF0;ar Helguson, &#x201C;Helguson, son of Helga&#x201D;.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_b373f5cb-06e7-4ccc-99ae-8d68d09afc00" id="_b373f5cb-06e7-4ccc-99ae-8d68d09afc00"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#xD6;rvar &#xDE;&#xF3;reyjarson Sm&#xE1;rason. (&#xD6;rvar, son of &#xDE;&#xF3;rey, son of Sm&#xE1;ri)</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e3c701f8-2707-4157-ae10-53e23d68a5e4" id="_e3c701f8-2707-4157-ae10-53e23d68a5e4"></a>Some family names do exist in Iceland, most commonly adaptations from last name
patronyms Icelanders took up when living abroad.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_34f18265-2ae1-483c-93e4-dcd2127915b0" id="_34f18265-2ae1-483c-93e4-dcd2127915b0"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  4</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Geir Haarde, Ei&#xF0;ur Sm&#xE1;ri Gu&#xF0;johnsen, Anita Briem.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_d62f86bc-6797-463e-b9de-00da162c8bff" id="_d62f86bc-6797-463e-b9de-00da162c8bff"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  5</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Nobel Prize-winning author Halld&#xF3;r Laxness, born as Halld&#xF3;r Gu&#xF0;j&#xF3;nsson.</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_indian" id="_indian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.18 Indian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_indonesian" id="_indonesian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.19 Indonesian</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_94b8ce66-e4a7-4456-befc-6750dc539937" id="_94b8ce66-e4a7-4456-befc-6750dc539937"></a>given name(s)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_701c6904-0f18-47a8-94ac-8a48ed1c3b03" id="_701c6904-0f18-47a8-94ac-8a48ed1c3b03"></a>Indonesians generally use given names without a family name.
The majority of Indonesians do not have family names. Rather,
their given names are geographically and culturally specific.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_f302124f-ba75-4c42-aaec-898b6294356c" id="_f302124f-ba75-4c42-aaec-898b6294356c"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Mulyono, the original name of Joko Widodo.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_56b873ca-b981-4402-90df-29f7456835c7" id="_56b873ca-b981-4402-90df-29f7456835c7"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Kusno Sosrodihardjo.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_38f046d2-1f4b-461f-a536-f4b3293550b5" id="_38f046d2-1f4b-461f-a536-f4b3293550b5"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Fransiskus Xaverius Hadi Rudyatmo</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_2bb72e78-9be8-4d30-98c0-cb455dd6f28a" id="_2bb72e78-9be8-4d30-98c0-cb455dd6f28a"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  4</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Sudono Salim</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_d14b3fde-a345-45c3-8a5b-cd307ad37e3b" id="_d14b3fde-a345-45c3-8a5b-cd307ad37e3b"></a>Some given names include a family name or a patronymic.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c5d7fd7b-ff5b-4c41-a482-faf944f46386" id="_c5d7fd7b-ff5b-4c41-a482-faf944f46386"></a>Indonesian names usually fall into one of the following categories:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo20;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    Mononymic names
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo20;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    Polynymic names without a family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo20;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    Polynymic names with a family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo20;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    Polynymic names with patronymic
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_6af96caf-0059-4e23-a6d4-cce7f637d6a5" id="_6af96caf-0059-4e23-a6d4-cce7f637d6a5"></a>An Indonesian name is often mis-represented in other cultures, such as:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo21;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    Netherlands: the word &#x201C;Onbekend&#x201D; (&#x201C;unknown&#x201D;) is assigned as a last name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo21;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    Germany: the one-word name is used as both given name and surname
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo21;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    US: &#x201C;Fnu&#x201D; (family name unknown) is assigned as the first or given name, &#x201C;Lnu&#x201D; (last name unknown) is assigned as the family, surname or last name,
or the name is duplicated as the surname.
  </p>
</div>
        <div><a name="_iranian" id="_iranian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.20 Iranian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_iraqi" id="_iraqi"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.21 Iraqi</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_italian" id="_italian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.22 Italian</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_4b8730c8-b752-45a9-8f13-74556476efa7" id="_4b8730c8-b752-45a9-8f13-74556476efa7"></a>given name(s) + family name</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_005d044f-61b9-4344-b5b7-7abea68f3193" id="_005d044f-61b9-4344-b5b7-7abea68f3193"></a>A name in Italian consists of a given name (nome) and a surname (cognome).
Surnames are normally written after given names.</p></div>
        <div><a name="_japanese" id="_japanese"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.23 Japanese</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e2248628-fbdd-42bf-b3cb-3b6be5951e39" id="_e2248628-fbdd-42bf-b3cb-3b6be5951e39"></a>family name + given name(s)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_211c1903-78ac-4b55-9edb-a0225cde1968" id="_211c1903-78ac-4b55-9edb-a0225cde1968"></a>Japanese names usually consist of a family name (surname),
followed by a given name.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_57935f93-2b1c-4964-8dc8-f54faca9c14d" id="_57935f93-2b1c-4964-8dc8-f54faca9c14d"></a>Japanese names are usually written in kanji,
where characters are logographic, but each with a variety of
possible Japanese pronunciations. Therefore
often names cannot in general be spelled or
pronounced unless both the spelling and pronunciation are given.</p>
<span style="MsoCommentReference" target="2" class="commentLink" from="" to=""><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:9.0pt" xml:lang="EN-GB"><a style="mso-comment-reference:SMC_2;mso-comment-date:20190724T000000Z"></a><span style="mso-special-character:comment" target="2"></span></span></span>
<div class="example"><a name="_2410db67-af13-48bf-ac31-cbec239ce01a" id="_2410db67-af13-48bf-ac31-cbec239ce01a"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x5927;&#x7FD4; is traditionally pronounced &#x201C;Hiroto&#x201D;, but can also be pronounced as
&#x201C;Haruto&#x201D;, &#x201C;Yamato&#x201D;, &#x201C;Taiga&#x201D;, &#x201C;Sora&#x201D;, &#x201C;Taito&#x201D;, &#x201C;Daito&#x201D;, and
&#x201C;Masato&#x201D;.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_05b60e74-5101-4bc7-ae0c-7c47aef731bc" id="_05b60e74-5101-4bc7-ae0c-7c47aef731bc"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x5927;&#x548C; can be read as Daiwa or Yamato.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_f5909197-c7b6-42da-9f15-0eb146883dc6" id="_f5909197-c7b6-42da-9f15-0eb146883dc6"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x6771;&#x6D77;&#x6797; can be read as T&#x14D;kairin or Sh&#x14D;ji</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_2e303166-b783-4f76-bd12-64db1cf02899" id="_2e303166-b783-4f76-bd12-64db1cf02899"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  4</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;&#x4E2D;&#x5C71;&#x6A35;&#x201D; (Nakayama Sho), the Japanese pseudonym of
&#x201C;Sun Yat Sen&#x201D;, where &#x201C;&#x4E2D;&#x5C71;&#x201D; is the family name, &#x201C;&#x6A35;&#x201D; the given name.</p></div>
<div><a name="_japanese_immigrants_in_brazil" id="_japanese_immigrants_in_brazil"></a><p class="h3Annex">B.23.1 Japanese immigrants in Brazil</p><p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table B.24</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_ab561532-55d8-4de1-982a-589725b2333c" id="_ab561532-55d8-4de1-982a-589725b2333c"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Akemi</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Denise</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Sameshima</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">given name</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">given name</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table B.25</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_b4e417cd-8833-47ca-b0f4-480840010b34" id="_b4e417cd-8833-47ca-b0f4-480840010b34"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Yuri</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Vanessa</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Ohara</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">given name</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">given name</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_jewish" id="_jewish"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.24 Jewish</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_23e2b144-e3c8-44d3-930e-73e5a8eebc55" id="_23e2b144-e3c8-44d3-930e-73e5a8eebc55"></a>given name(s) + family names</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_cc44ec68-8624-4bc7-8079-d1b6d124f6d4" id="_cc44ec68-8624-4bc7-8079-d1b6d124f6d4"></a>or</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_13466809-be30-44c2-843f-3cf4346c10bc" id="_13466809-be30-44c2-843f-3cf4346c10bc"></a>given name(s) + patronymic name</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1b4736d7-9502-46b3-a186-6c4311415528" id="_1b4736d7-9502-46b3-a186-6c4311415528"></a>Modern Jewish names include Hebrew patronymic names as well as family names.</p></div>
        <div><a name="_korean" id="_korean"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.25 Korean</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_9dc96d9b-b1ba-4d2c-8c5e-a43a4a1135cb" id="_9dc96d9b-b1ba-4d2c-8c5e-a43a4a1135cb"></a>family name + given name(s)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ad27d484-e331-4e7f-b128-1b0158420950" id="_ad27d484-e331-4e7f-b128-1b0158420950"></a>A Korean name consists of a family name followed by a given name, as used by
the Korean people in both South Korea and North Korea.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_136cf3aa-80f2-42ce-aadf-fe9f9cd22353" id="_136cf3aa-80f2-42ce-aadf-fe9f9cd22353"></a>In the Korean language,
ireum or seongmyeong usually refers to the family name (seong) and given name
(myeong) together.</p></div>
        <div><a name="_kurdish" id="_kurdish"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.26 Kurdish</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_latvian" id="_latvian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.27 Latvian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_lithuanian" id="_lithuanian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.28 Lithuanian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_macedonian" id="_macedonian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.29 Macedonian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_manchu" id="_manchu"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.30 Manchu</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_a93ed9eb-d3ee-4a9c-a4aa-da44751e249c" id="_a93ed9eb-d3ee-4a9c-a4aa-da44751e249c"></a>given name(s) (+ optional family name)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3053e4ec-dd71-4f0d-9604-88f6ee2cb764" id="_3053e4ec-dd71-4f0d-9604-88f6ee2cb764"></a>or</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_6d094dd1-33ad-4cf5-bcb4-bd1e977cdad5" id="_6d094dd1-33ad-4cf5-bcb4-bd1e977cdad5"></a>(optional family name +) given name(s)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_5581e372-f2cb-4b00-b364-27d708df79bb" id="_5581e372-f2cb-4b00-b364-27d708df79bb"></a>Manchus are called only by their given names.
Manchu clan names (&#x201C;hala&#x201D;) are not used with their personal names,
but occasionally a family name is used.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_d10e7000-2d77-4304-a3de-2ab9d4fbbac8" id="_d10e7000-2d77-4304-a3de-2ab9d4fbbac8"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Tuli&#x161;en&#x201D;</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_40a32fea-641a-4507-b924-1246a44270d5" id="_40a32fea-641a-4507-b924-1246a44270d5"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Hiowan Ye&#x201D; (&#x7384;&#x70E8;)</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_c32caf54-2c22-44fe-b0d4-251bddf72dfc" id="_c32caf54-2c22-44fe-b0d4-251bddf72dfc"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Aisin-Gioro Ulhicun&#x201D;, linguist. The family name is &#x201C;Aisin-Gioro&#x201D;.</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_mongolian" id="_mongolian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.31 Mongolian</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_6ea926ba-13f8-4042-bb6a-d1be9379bd0d" id="_6ea926ba-13f8-4042-bb6a-d1be9379bd0d"></a>given name (+ optional clan name or family name)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_9fff1a1a-8895-4c40-ba81-fb26d527f2d1" id="_9fff1a1a-8895-4c40-ba81-fb26d527f2d1"></a>or</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c2f03ff0-e7f1-4021-a1e5-c9ba62e8d931" id="_c2f03ff0-e7f1-4021-a1e5-c9ba62e8d931"></a>genonymic + given name</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_bbe1aa07-11ec-4ec8-a9bd-ec7a4cca22df" id="_bbe1aa07-11ec-4ec8-a9bd-ec7a4cca22df"></a>Mongolian names traditionally consists of only one personal name.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_21e376ff-74bd-42f2-bed7-721595a3826d" id="_21e376ff-74bd-42f2-bed7-721595a3826d"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x41E;&#x442;&#x440;&#x44F;&#x434;&#x44B;&#x43D; &#x413;&#x4AF;&#x43D;&#x434;&#x44D;&#x433;&#x43C;&#x430;&#x430; (&#x201C;Otryadyn G&#xFC;ndegmaa&#x201D;), a Mongolian shooter, has &#x201C;Otryadyn&#x201D; as a patronym, &#x201C;G&#xFC;ndegmaa&#x201D; as given name.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_b33ea41d-3a3a-4fa5-97d7-da62a56a2fb9" id="_b33ea41d-3a3a-4fa5-97d7-da62a56a2fb9"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x425;&#x430;&#x43B;&#x442;&#x43C;&#x430;&#x430;&#x433;&#x438;&#x439;&#x43D; &#x411;&#x430;&#x442;&#x442;&#x443;&#x43B;&#x433;&#x430; (&#x201C;Khaltmaagiin Battulga&#x201D;), President of Mongolia.</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_nigerian" id="_nigerian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.32 Nigerian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_pakistani" id="_pakistani"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.33 Pakistani</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_portuguese" id="_portuguese"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.34 Portuguese</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1769acf2-3ec6-4361-a4f8-83059822d5c1" id="_1769acf2-3ec6-4361-a4f8-83059822d5c1"></a>given name(s) + mother&#x2019;s patronymic name(s) + father&#x2019;s patronymic name(s)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c043c754-35fd-48f5-b2f1-efe67db09950" id="_c043c754-35fd-48f5-b2f1-efe67db09950"></a>Portuguese often have two personal names, although the first may at times be used on its own.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_2613813a-67bf-434e-bdf8-7fd10c060dd0" id="_2613813a-67bf-434e-bdf8-7fd10c060dd0"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>George Agostinho Baptista da Silva.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_37d8be9e-096a-4afc-94ed-6f953197d7c6" id="_37d8be9e-096a-4afc-94ed-6f953197d7c6"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Ant&#xF3;nio Caetano de Abreu Freire Egas Moniz, Nobel prize winner. He was the child of Fernando de Pina Rezende Abreu and Maria do Rosario de Almeida e Sousa.</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_romanian" id="_romanian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.35 Romanian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_russian" id="_russian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.36 Russian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_sikh" id="_sikh"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.37 Sikh</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_sinhalese" id="_sinhalese"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.38 Sinhalese</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_slavic" id="_slavic"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.39 Slavic</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2d6e015e-1df5-44d0-ab7a-9a175d419af0" id="_2d6e015e-1df5-44d0-ab7a-9a175d419af0"></a>given name + patronymic name + family name</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3835bf02-6fbd-49ab-ae2e-19ecb0ea6983" id="_3835bf02-6fbd-49ab-ae2e-19ecb0ea6983"></a>Slavic naming applies to Russian, Ukrainian, Belorussian,
Bulgaria, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Serbia and Macedonia,
as well as some populations of Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Uzbekistan and Turkmenistan.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_01972604-48b1-4461-92ce-842779b27422" id="_01972604-48b1-4461-92ce-842779b27422"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x418;&#x432;&#x430;&#x301;&#x43D; &#x41A;&#x43E;&#x43D;&#x441;&#x442;&#x430;&#x43D;&#x442;&#x438;&#x301;&#x43D;&#x43E;&#x432;&#x438;&#x447; &#x410;&#x439;&#x432;&#x430;&#x437;&#x43E;&#x301;&#x432;&#x441;&#x43A;&#x438;&#x439; (&#x201C;Ivan Konstantinovich Aivazovsky&#x201D;). Ivan is the given name, Konstantinovich the patronymic name, Aivazovsky the family name.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_2b381c03-f3aa-4526-b897-9137e40924e4" id="_2b381c03-f3aa-4526-b897-9137e40924e4"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x41E;&#x43B;&#x435;&#x43A;&#x441;&#x430;&#x43D;&#x434;&#x440; &#x406;&#x432;&#x430;&#x43D;&#x43E;&#x432;&#x438;&#x447; &#x411;&#x456;&#x43B;&#x430;&#x448;, (&#x201C;Oleksandr Ivanovych Bilash&#x201D;).  Oleksandr is the given name, Ivanovych the patronymic name, Bilash the family name.</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_slovenian" id="_slovenian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.40 Slovenian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_somali" id="_somali"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.41 Somali</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_spanish" id="_spanish"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.42 Spanish</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_477a8e94-ab8a-467b-9ce3-353c08b015c0" id="_477a8e94-ab8a-467b-9ce3-353c08b015c0"></a>given name(s) + father&#x2019;s patronymic name(s) + mother&#x2019;s patronymic name(s)</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_e85f0e5b-d57a-4a6b-bbde-2af19a5ed9fe" id="_e85f0e5b-d57a-4a6b-bbde-2af19a5ed9fe"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Salvador de Madariaga y Rojo, Spanish diplomat, writer, historian and pacifist. Child of Dar&#xED;o Jos&#xE9; de Madariaga&#x200B; and Mar&#xED;a Ascensi&#xF3;n Rojo.</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_tamil" id="_tamil"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.43 Tamil</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_thai" id="_thai"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.44 Thai</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_c7f49197-92b2-402c-a6c8-f539ae8f286b" id="_c7f49197-92b2-402c-a6c8-f539ae8f286b"></a>given name(s) + family name</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_952bb1a5-aa7a-4441-b7f5-61e424fa9a5c" id="_952bb1a5-aa7a-4441-b7f5-61e424fa9a5c"></a>Modern Thai names are composed of given names followed by the family name.
Prior to 1913, family names were not required.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_938306bd-513e-4f49-94cc-ef4efc7d2a1e" id="_938306bd-513e-4f49-94cc-ef4efc7d2a1e"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#xE0A;&#xE27;&#xE19; &#xE2B;&#xE25;&#xE35;&#xE01;&#xE20;&#xE31;&#xE22; (&#x201C;Chuan Likphai&#x201D;)</p></div></div>
        <div><a name="_turkish" id="_turkish"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.45 Turkish</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_ukrainian" id="_ukrainian"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.46 Ukrainian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_vietnamese" id="_vietnamese"></a><p class="h2Annex">B.47 Vietnamese</p><table class="dl"><tr><td valign="top" align="left"><p align="left" style="margin-left:0pt;text-align:left;" class="MsoNormal">Full</p></td><td valign="top">
    <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_cb2f100c-6d3e-4ffc-a014-fbd27f308776" id="_cb2f100c-6d3e-4ffc-a014-fbd27f308776"></a>family name (+ optional additional name(s)) + given name</p>
  </td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left"><p align="left" style="margin-left:0pt;text-align:left;" class="MsoNormal">Abbreviated</p></td><td valign="top">
    <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e655c202-d280-4f36-abae-231f89378180" id="_e655c202-d280-4f36-abae-231f89378180"></a>given name</p>
  </td></tr></table>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_4d9f7a21-a103-4044-86f0-62ec0e83aafe" id="_4d9f7a21-a103-4044-86f0-62ec0e83aafe"></a>Vietnamese personal names are names used by those from Vietnam and the Vietnamese diaspora overseas.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ba02d279-d0b6-443c-8f9a-19428f2cd224" id="_ba02d279-d0b6-443c-8f9a-19428f2cd224"></a>Vietnamese names consist of a family name (T&#xEA;n, &#x20E1B;),
followed by a given name (H&#x1ECD;, /&#x22A5C;).
Between the family name and given name,
one or more additional names may be present.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b8787a83-8129-4d3e-bf2f-7ca872fdad83" id="_b8787a83-8129-4d3e-bf2f-7ca872fdad83"></a>Vietnamese additional names can be a
middle name (t&#xEA;n &#x111;&#x1EC7;m),
generational name,
or clan distinguisher name. The middle name, for identification purposes, can be omitted.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e74f6469-a13f-48d6-b1ad-c098180653d4" id="_e74f6469-a13f-48d6-b1ad-c098180653d4"></a>Courtesy names are also allowed, separate from the given name.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_d0e19f7a-1e11-458b-976b-f0db948f3cc7" id="_d0e19f7a-1e11-458b-976b-f0db948f3cc7"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n Sinh Cung&#x201D;; where &#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n&#x201D; is the family name, &#x201C;Sinh Cung&#x201D; the given name. The birth name of &#x201C;H&#x1ED3; Ch&#xED; Minh&#x201D;.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_d5405928-4701-4a88-81ce-5b3cfbcaac1a" id="_d5405928-4701-4a88-81ce-5b3cfbcaac1a"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;H&#x1ED3; Ch&#xED; Minh&#x201D;; where &#x201C;H&#x1ED3;&#x201D; is the family name, &#x201C;Ch&#xED; Minh&#x201D; the given name.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_af489377-9407-4eee-9732-86158a0319f0" id="_af489377-9407-4eee-9732-86158a0319f0"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n T&#x1EA5;t Th&#xE0;nh&#x201D; is another name of &#x201C;H&#x1ED3; Ch&#xED; Minh&#x201D;, where &#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n&#x201D; is the family name, &#x201C;T&#x1EA5;t Th&#xE0;nh&#x201D; the given name.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_23bcfad3-df3a-4c63-b73b-bae29cc07e17" id="_23bcfad3-df3a-4c63-b73b-bae29cc07e17"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  4</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n &#xC1;i Qu&#x1ED1;c&#x201D; (&#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n the Patriot&#x201D;) is a pseudonym of &#x201C;H&#x1ED3; Ch&#xED; Minh&#x201D;, where &#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n&#x201D; is the family name, &#x201C;&#xC1;i Qu&#x1ED1;c&#x201D; the given name.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_001e4c89-8f5c-4029-a529-738cdeabd986" id="_001e4c89-8f5c-4029-a529-738cdeabd986"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  5</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n V&#x103;n Hu&#x1EC7;&#x201D;; where &#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n&#x201D; is the family name, &#x201C;V&#x103;n&#x201D; the middle name, &#x201C;Hu&#x1EC7;&#x201D; the given name. &#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n V&#x103;n Hu&#x1EC7;&#x201D; is also called &#x201C;Nguy&#x1EC5;n Hu&#x1EC7;&#x201D;.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_355cb874-bc59-4a8a-81b6-3bc327c1cb57" id="_355cb874-bc59-4a8a-81b6-3bc327c1cb57"></a><p class="MsoNormal"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  6</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;L&#xEA; T&#x1B0; Th&#xE0;nh&#x201D;, where &#x201C;L&#xEA;&#x201D; is the family name, &#x201C;T&#x1B0; Th&#xE0;nh&#x201D; the given name. &#x201C;L&#xEA; T&#x1B0; Th&#xE0;nh&#x201D; also has a courtesy name &#x201C;L&#xEA; H&#x1EA1;o&#x201D;, where &#x201C;L&#xEA;&#x201D; is the family name, &#x201C;H&#x1EA1;o&#x201D; the courtesy name.</p></div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="MsoNormal">
        <br clear="all" style="mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:always"/>
      </p>
      <div>
        <h1 class="Section3">Bibliography</h1>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO9945" id="ISO9945"></a>[1]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO/IEC/IEEE 9945:2009, <i> Portable Operating System Interface (POSIX&#xAE;) Base Specifications, Issue 7</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO19788-5" id="ISO19788-5"></a>[2]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO/IEC 19788-5:2012, <i> Learning, education and training</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO12234-3" id="ISO12234-3"></a>[3]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO 12234-3:2016, <i> Removable memory</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO9075-1" id="ISO9075-1"></a>[4]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO/IEC 9075-1:2016, <i> Database languages</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO14813-5" id="ISO14813-5"></a>[5]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO 14813-5:2010, <i> Reference model architecture(s) for the ITS sector</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO14198" id="ISO14198"></a>[6]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO/TS 14198:2012, <i> Ergonomic aspects of transport information and control systems</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO29003" id="ISO29003"></a>[7]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO/IEC TS 29003:2018, <i> Security techniques</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO14105" id="ISO14105"></a>[8]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO/TR 14105:2011, <i> Change management for successful electronic document management system (EDMS) implementation</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO20944-1" id="ISO20944-1"></a>[9]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO/IEC 20944-1:2013, <i> Metadata Registries Interoperability and Bindings (MDR-IB)</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO5127" id="ISO5127"></a>[10]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO 5127:2017, <i> Foundation and vocabulary</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO31320" id="ISO31320"></a>[11]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO/IEC/IEEE 31320-2:2012, <i> Modeling Languages</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="iso639" id="iso639"></a>[12]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO 639, <i> Code for the representation of names of languages</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO639-3" id="ISO639-3"></a>[13]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO 639-3, <i> Codes for the representation of names of languages</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="ISO15961" id="ISO15961"></a>[14]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO/IEC 15961:2004, <i> Radio frequency identification (RFID) for item management</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="iso15924" id="iso15924"></a>[15]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>ISO 15924:2004, <i> Codes for the representation of names of scripts</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="rfc2046" id="rfc2046"></a>[16]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>IETF RFC 2046, <i>Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) Part Two: Media Types</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="rfc3986" id="rfc3986"></a>[17]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>IETF RFC 3986, <i>Uniform Resource Identifier (URI): Generic Syntax</i></p>
        <p class="Biblio"><a name="rfc8288" id="rfc8288"></a>[18]<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>IETF RFC 8288, <i>Web Linking</i></p>
      </div>
